## Public surface and impact

- **Rust library & CLI:** Queue resolver/extraction/check logic, config v2 schema (`queues.unboundedJobRetention`, `queues.jobStateAsRecord`), `CheckSeverity`, standalone `queues check` advisory exit behavior, and aggregate `check` advisory demotion.
- **N-API & `.d.ts`:** `analyzeProject()` / `queuesCheck()` parity for the new options and `severity`; exported `QueueJobRetentionKey`, `QueueUnboundedJobRetentionOptions`, `QueueUnboundedJobRetentionConfig`, `QueueJobStateAsRecordOptions`, `QueueJobStateAsRecordConfig`, and `QueueCheckSeverity` in `packages/no-mistakes/*.d.ts` and `exported-type-names.json`.
- **Docs & skills:** Updated `docs/configuration/queues.md`, `docs/cli/queues-check.md`, `docs/cli/queues.md`, `docs/node-api.md`, `docs/feature-parity.md`, and `plugins/no-mistakes-rules/skills/queue-rules/SKILL.md`.
- **Fixtures & snapshots:** Added saved fixtures under `test-cases/queue-ast-hop/{workspace-exports-3953,unbounded-retention,job-state-as-record,job-options-followups}` and `fixtures/check/{queue-retention-config,queue-job-state-config}`, with committed `.snap` files and unit/CLI/N-API parity tests.

## Merge with main

### Merge `08164e39b` (including #3992 `0f6511c862`)

- `crates/no-mistakes/src/queue/extract_model.rs` (content conflict): kept both sides' `FileFacts` fields — this PR's `unbounded_job_retention`, `job_state_sites`, and `job_state_as_record` alongside #3992's `worker_class_imports`, `worker_class_namespaces`, `worker_constructed_aliases`, and `worker_constructed_namespaces`.
- `crates/no-mistakes/src/queue/extract_prefilter.rs` (content conflict): kept this PR's `STATIC_NEEDLES` table (including `getJob`, `getFailed`, `getCompleted`, `getJobs`) while keeping #3992's narrowed `rateLimit` prefilter (`contains_bytes(haystack, b"rateLimit") && contains_bytes(haystack, b"import")`) outside `STATIC_NEEDLES`.
- `packages/no-mistakes/index.d.ts` (post-merge `oxlint` `max-lines` fix): removed the duplicate `export type { QueueCheckSeverity } from "./queue-report-types";` line so `index.d.ts` stays within 200 lines; `QueueCheckSeverity` remains publicly exported via `export * from "./types"` → `report-types.d.ts` → `queue-report-types.d.ts` (verified by `packages/no-mistakes/scripts/api.test.js`).

### Merge `6ee88425c` (including #3990)

- `crates/no-mistakes/src/check_runner/results.rs` (content conflict): kept #3990's `warnings::collect(root, facts, config, react_warning, &mut completed)` before destructuring `CompletedDomainChecks` so queue analysis warnings surface in aggregate `check`, while preserving this PR's `advisories::demote(..., &mut queues.findings, ...)`.
- `crates/no-mistakes/src/check_runner/results/empty.rs` (post-merge cleanup): removed the unused `empty::collect_warnings` helper superseded by `warnings::collect`.
- `crates/no-mistakes/src/queue/mod.rs` (content conflict): kept both sides' `graph_model` re-exports (`CheckSeverity` alongside `format_aggregate_warning`, `format_diagnostic`, and `CheckReport`).
- `crates/no-mistakes/src/queues.rs` (content conflict): kept #3990's `render::print_diagnostics_stderr` and `render::print_check(..., *include_diagnostics)` calls alongside this PR's `report.check.iter().all(CheckFinding::is_advisory)` exit-code logic (importing `CheckFinding`).
- `docs/cli/queues.md` (content conflict): combined both `queues check` summary entries (per-process worker rate limits, unbounded job retention, advisory queue job state usage, and `--include-diagnostics`).
- `packages/no-mistakes/scripts/api-tests/exported-type-names.json` (content conflict): kept `QueueCheckOptions`, `QueueCheckReport` (#3990), and `QueueCheckSeverity` (#3973) in sorted order.

Re-ran the `unbounded-job-retention` and `job-state-as-record` `no-mistakes queues check` commands above against the merged binary; outputs and exit codes are unchanged. All committed queue unit and CLI snapshots pass with `INSTA_UPDATE=no`.
